WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:21.320
Recently, we’ve published a lot of videos
about Venezuela and the terrible political

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.250
situation that this country is facing.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.180
We’ve told you how they got to this point;
the basic characteristics of this narco-dictatorship

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.050
and how the revolution involved, the Bolivarian
revolution, has condemned most Venezuelans

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.330
to poverty, even causing one of the greatest
exoduses in history.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:43.660
“Venezuelan refugees now number 3.4 million;
humanitarian implications massive, UN warns”.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.660
UN news)

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.960
However, while events are rushing at warp-speed
with this man, Juan Guaido, leading a firm

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.010
opposition against the Maduro regime, we thought
that we needed to make a general review of

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.700
a fundamental issue:

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.670
Who are Nicolás Maduro’s main allies?

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.689
Who are the players that continue, despite
everything, to support this regime, and why?

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:06.079
What are their interests?

00:01:06.079 --> 00:01:08.820
“Cuba is yours and belongs to everyone”)

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.280
, It may seem incredible given the current
circumstances, but the Chavez regime continues

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.650
to have some very formidable allies.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.260
Listen up because these are the four most
influential partners, the four strongest allies

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.430
that the Venezuelan regime still has.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:32.030
(4th - TODAY FOR YOU, TOMORROW FOR ME)

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.140
2010 saw the beginning of a beautiful friendship
Or perhaps it would be more accurate to call

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.799
it a hateful fellowship – you decide.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:44.190
That year Nicolás Maduro traveled to Turkey
as Venezuela’s Chancellor.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.159
There he met current Turkish president Tayyip
Erdogan.

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:53.159
“These are two politicians who feel attacked
by the West and the relationship is predominantly

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:57.450
emotionally-based [...] Erdogan doesn’t
forget that Maduro was one of the first leaders

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:02.600
who supported him during the attempted coup
of July 15th, 2016.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.090
Now Turkey is returning the support they received”.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.159
Mehmet Ozkan, Centre for Global Policy in
Washington)

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:13.390
So we can understand this better, this relationship
goes something like this:

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.840
Hey, look, it turns out that the rest of the
world has has it in for us, they say we are

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:22.290
authoritarian, as if bringing about order
were a bad thing, they say we don’t respect

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.909
freedom of the press.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:28.269
So how about if you support me and I support
you.

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:32.829
“These populist and authoritarian leaders
are seeking to develop man-to-man relations,

00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:36.010
rather than relying on institutions, bureaucracies
or rules."

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.090
Mehmet Ozkan)

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.260
The fact is that since the Turkish coup d'état
took place – or as is suspected, the auto-coup

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.500
d'état – trade between both countries has
multiplied thirteenfold.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:52.689
In 2018 alone, exports from Venezuela to Turkey
surpassed one billion dollars.

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:58.499
And no, this wasn’t industrial or even agricultural
products, not at all.

00:02:58.499 --> 00:03:02.580
I’m talking about the last source of foreign
currency with which the Venezuelan regime

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.050
has attempted to stay alive.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.379
I'm talking about gold.

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:08.779
“1,480 tons of gold.

00:03:08.779 --> 00:03:09.779
To speculate, me.”)

00:03:09.779 --> 00:03:14.209
Turkey has become a satellite headquarters
e for refining, certifying and distributing

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:15.689
Venezuelan gold.

00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:20.760
It is the perfect laundry so to speak, allowing
Nicolás Maduro’s government to continue

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.480
to obtain foreign currency.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.950
This is becoming more and more complicated,
however, especially after the collapse that

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.749
the oil “industry” has been experiencing.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:35.419
Venezuela Oil Exports Slump to a 28-Year Low.

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:37.449
Bloomberg)

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:43.209
Apparently, the agreement that Venezuela and
Turkey signed, would be allowing Caracas to

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:46.480
evade the United States’ sanctions.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.060
Mysterious Turkish Firm Helped Maduro Move
$900 Million in Gold.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.060
Bloomberg)

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.409
In the last few months, sightings of private
Russian and Turkish jets have been frequent

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:59.779
at Caracas airport; some of them, by the way,
were owned by Ciner, a mining company that

00:03:59.779 --> 00:04:01.779
is very close to President Erdogan.

00:04:01.779 --> 00:04:06.129
Well, what is suspected is that these planes
are arriving in Caracas to get gold from the

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:08.189
country in a rather shadyway.

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:12.089
I’m sure you can guess where a lot of this
gold will end up.

00:04:12.089 --> 00:04:19.599
“There are a lot of bandits out there, taking
advantage of their post to rob the people.”)

00:04:19.599 --> 00:04:21.549
But relationships go beyond that.

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:26.290
In December 2018, not long ago at all, Erdogan
starred in the first visit of a Turkish head

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.830
of state to Venezuela.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.180
During this trip, commercial agreements with
a value of more than 5 billion dollars were

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:35.970
signed and the creation of joint ventures
for the exploration and exploitation of coal,

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:40.810
gold and oil were announced.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.290
For example, it’s highly significant that
the Turkish food industry provides about 70%

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:49.390
of the food that the Venezuelan government
distributes under the CLAP program, these

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:54.300
are food bags that are delivered to families
monthly as a means to gain some popular support

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.880
“You can imagine how Venezuela would be
without the CLAPs.”)

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.250
But, let's move on.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:07.940
“Fellow President, the honour guard is ready.”)

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.740
(3rd: WHAT ABOUT MY THINGS?)

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.730
It is well known that throughout the Bolivarian
Revolution, Cuba’s role has been extremely

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:31.150
significant.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.050
Cuba first supplied Hugo Chávez and then
Nicolás Maduro, with paramilitary forces,

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:40.300
protection, intelligence teams... practically
everything that the Venezuelan bigwigs needed

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.260
to consolidate their power.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:48.190
Venezuela is nine times larger than Cuba,
has three times its population and its economy

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.530
is four times larger.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:54.270
The country is home to the world's main oil
reserves, however, some crucial functions

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:58.980
of the Venezuelan state have been delegated
to Cuban officials, or are directly controlled

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.590
by Havana.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.220
Moisés Naím)

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:13.150
It may be controversial to say so, but Cuba
has basically become a supermarket of terror

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.210
for all dictators.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:18.970
According to the Secretary General of the
Organization of American States, Luis Almagro,

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:24.120
there are between 21,000 and 46,000 Cubans
in Venezuela.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:28.600
Rubio: Cuban agents direct repression in Ureña,
Venezuela, El Nuevo Herald)

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:33.890
“Cuba is responsible for repression and
torture in Venezuela” Luis Almagro, Secretary

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.840
General of the OAS)

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:41.940
Of course, none of this has come for free.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:52.800
You see, in exchange for supplying doctors
and paramilitary forces,, Cuba has received

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.840
a lot of oil in more than advantageous conditions
from the Venezuelan government in recent years.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.400
In fact, during the Bolivarian Revolution,
the Cuban economy has been very dependent

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:08.220
on Venezuela, although not as much as with
the Soviet Union.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:18.530
However, as things continue to progress, and
although they still seem to be playing a key

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:22.960
role in the repression today, the island simply
doesn’t have enough economic resources to

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.100
keep the narco-Chavez regime on its feet.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:30.170
What I mean is that in the future, Cuba’s
biggest role may be only to give refuge to

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:38.760
Nicolás Maduro and his cronies, so long as
the DEA doesn’t capture them first.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:44.440
(2nd BUSINESS IS BUSINESS)

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:49.920
If you follow VisualPolitik regularly, you
may know this well, we’ve focused a lot

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.150
on the Caracas-Beijing relationship.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:57.200
And no, this isn’t an ideological issue...
it was, is and probably will be, with or without

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.120
Maduro, a pure matter of business.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.990
“Oil is the most fundamental reason why
China and Venezuela joined forces.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:11.250
China needed a lot of oil and Venezuela had
it [...] The relationship flourished since

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:18.410
then and both built ties based on “oil financing
agreements” Matt Ferchen, Carnegie-Tsinghua

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.120
Center for Global Policy.)

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.860
You see, the first oil loan agreements between
China and Venezuela date back to 2007.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:34.290
“Venezuela has established itself at this
point as the country in which China has the

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.789
highest level of investment in Latin America.

00:08:36.789 --> 00:08:39.649
We’re first in Chinese investments in Latin
America.”)

00:08:39.649 --> 00:08:44.860
For Hugo Chávez's Venezuela, these agreements
meant fresh, constant and sound cash flow

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:45.860
for his revolution.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:49.660
For China, on the other hand, gaining access
to the Latin American country’s huge energy

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.830
resources was something that the Chinese economy
needed at all costs.

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:59.350
Their oil consumption rates increased year
after year and they needed to secure their

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.550
supply.

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:11.920
And we aren’t talking about small numbers:

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:17.300
According to data from the Centre for Inter-American
Studies and Boston University, between 2007

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:22.620
and 2018, China lent the Latin American country
almost 70 billion dollars.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.959
Today, the debt seems to surpass 20 billion,
and to be fair we must say that Maduro hasn’t

00:09:27.959 --> 00:09:30.209
exactly been a good payer.

00:09:30.209 --> 00:09:35.670
“And the financing schemes we have with
China don’t generate debt, Venezuela must

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.670
know this.”)

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.760
Beijing trusted that the Venezuelan authorities
would be able to do something productive with

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.279
all the money they had set on the table, at
the very least invest enough to maintain oil

00:09:44.279 --> 00:09:45.420
production levels.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.769
Beijing never imagined that the Venezuelan
government would be so disastrous.

00:09:48.769 --> 00:09:54.680
And so for the Chinese all this is fundamentally
a matter of business, leading to incidents

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:58.660
like this:

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:02.279
China sues Venezuela's oil company over unpaid
bills.

00:10:02.279 --> 00:10:03.279
CNN)

00:10:03.279 --> 00:10:08.850
In spite of everything, Beijing suspects that
their agreements could be endangered if there’s

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:13.220
a government change, which could mean not
charging part of the debt that Venezuela has

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:18.220
to pay in oil or even losing the privileged
access they are getting from Venezuela’s

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.220
huge reserves.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.980
It is precisely for this reason that one of
President Juan Guaido’s objectives seems

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:29.389
to be to assure the Chinese that whatever
happens, the past agreements will be respected.

00:10:29.389 --> 00:10:32.399
China Talks With Venezuela Opposition to Protect
Investments.

00:10:32.399 --> 00:10:33.470
The Wall Street Journal)

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:40.040
No matter how the situation evolves,” “China-Venezuela
cooperation should not be undermined.”Foreign

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.680
Ministry spokesman Geng Shuang)

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:47.459
In any case,, if you want to know more about
this relationship, don’t miss this video.

00:10:47.459 --> 00:10:54.089
And finally, we get to the last ally and what
may well be Nicolás Maduro’s last hope.

00:10:54.089 --> 00:11:00.899
(1st : A SPEARHEAD AGAINST THE WEST)

00:11:00.899 --> 00:11:06.259
Nowadays, Vladimir Putin's Russia is the biggest
international supporter that Nicolás Maduro’s

00:11:06.259 --> 00:11:08.949
regime has.

00:11:08.949 --> 00:11:12.949
In the last two decades, Russian companies
have secured important military contracts

00:11:12.949 --> 00:11:18.329
and since 2015, many rights to some of the
most significant oil and gas fields in Venezuela.

00:11:18.329 --> 00:11:21.209
And they have achieved all this at bargain
prices.

00:11:21.209 --> 00:11:22.470
Want an example?

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:28.309
Well... take a look.

00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:38.529
In exchange for a desperate 1.5 billion dollars
rescue, the Venezuelan government has set

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:43.740
49.9% of its stake in Citgo, PDVSA’s crown
jewel, an oil company that operates in the

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:48.660
United States, where it owns 3 refineries,
a huge gas pipeline network and almost 6,000

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.290
service stations, as warranty.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:55.389
If PDVSA doesn’t pay the 1.5 billion dollars
they owe to Rosneft and Gazprom, Venezuela

00:11:55.389 --> 00:11:59.959
could be forced to sell what is today its
most valuable industrial asset at a very low

00:11:59.959 --> 00:12:00.970
price.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.560
All for just 1.5 billion dollars.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:15.300
Just a second, 1.5 billion for half of Citgo,
which is worth much more, are you joking?

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:22.069
Welcome to Maduro’s ‘Desperation Sale’.

00:12:22.069 --> 00:12:26.379
The point is, folks, that Russia has become
the Venezuelan government’s number one supplier

00:12:26.379 --> 00:12:33.529
of weapons, military equipment and instruments
of repression:

00:12:33.529 --> 00:12:42.800
missiles, tanks, planes… in recent years,
the Bolivarian government has spent a lot

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.819
of money on Russian equipment.

00:12:44.819 --> 00:12:52.149
For Putin, Venezuela has meant a huge business
for his military industry, which is so important

00:12:52.149 --> 00:12:56.970
in Russia, but now he also sees it as an opportunity
to continue poking the West’s eye while

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:02.220
he increases his control over some of the
planet’s largest energy reserves.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:10.189
Anyway, folks, these are the four most important
allies on which Nicolás Maduro’s narco-dictatorship

00:13:10.189 --> 00:13:11.189
still counts.

00:13:11.189 --> 00:13:15.550
Also on the list would be countries like Bolivia,
Nicaragua or Belarus, but these have a much

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.199
smaller influence globally.

00:13:17.199 --> 00:13:21.350
As it stands, the Bolivarian government will
do anything it can to secure Russia, China

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:26.470
and Turkey’s - they already have Cuba’s
- full, expressed and firm support, even if

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.449
they have to sell what little remains in Venezuela.

00:13:29.449 --> 00:13:33.779
However... the political weakness and chaos
that the Chavez government has created is

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:37.850
so extreme that this may no longer have enough
to bargain with.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:43.019
Basically, with this video, we wanted to better
explain who continues to support this train

00:13:43.019 --> 00:13:44.260
wreck of a regime..

